<!--
    Kuna `iokitclasses on` (the typed classes) against `iokitclasses names`
    on an XNU kext.

    The fixture (gen_iokitcxx.py) is an arm64 MH_KEXT_BUNDLE whose
    initializer registers Base and Derived (0x30 bytes, a site.Derived
    kalloc_type view) through an unnamed OSMetaClass constructor. Derived's
    vtable holds an unnamed override of Base::m2 that reads the field at 0x10;
    Derived::Derived stores the vtable's address point and a field;
    Base::twice calls slot 4 of its own vtable; make_derived calls
    Derived::MetaClass::alloc.

    Pass 1 (`names`) is the bug: the override's this is void *a0 read by
    index, the constructor stores a raw constant, the virtual call is pointer
    arithmetic on a0 and the alloc returns nothing. Pass 2 (`on`, the default)
    types this as its class, the store as this->vtable = &Derived_vtable, the
    call as a named slot of this->vtable, and the alloc as returning Derived *.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">c0035fd6</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
